read costs one refused act, never a wrong one.\n  - The in-place form refuses `--role` and `--values` before it reads anything.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- The reds. The SHA-256 values of `2026-11-18-u3-red/1.txt` through `4.txt` equal the note's table. Each file shows one failed test in the named file: three in `application-upgrade.test.ts` (plain) and one in `screen-upgrade.test.ts` (native, the real sandbox Worker and screen service). Red 4 puts the presentation compare back into the matcher, and the screen read after an in-place upgrade then answers 404, not 200.\n- The gate. END b1f18993 passed at this head. The first line of `artroom-evidence/2026-11-18-u3-gate-2/gate.txt` names this head and tree c7d01d23 with 0 changed files. The log ends \"gate passed\" and \"exit=0\". Its pins stage checks the three new seals and the two open presentations.\n- Scope. The 20 artifacts name the head and equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 44330407 db539197`.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 2 checked, 0 flagged. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. No added line names a private path or another project. I ran no tests.\n- Version rule 163de663. Only the open Lending 0.6.0 and Counter 0.7.0 presentations move. No signed release changes.\n\n## Wake rate\n\nThe head adds no alarm, retry, reschedule or scheduled pass. The CLI adds per-command reads only: one item query, at most eight journal pages for an open in-place upgrade, and the existing submit. On the screen path, a request at a non-current presentation now reaches the room for 2 Durable Object requests and a 404, where the sandbox used to refuse it for 0. A request at the current presentation already costs the same 2, so the change gives no caller a cheaper or larger way to wake the room. Requests per room per hour do not change with no traffic.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One check of the presentation now lives in one place, the room's route, which already reads the installation for each request. The sandbox and the client match the installation, not a copy of its presentation, so an in-place upgrade needs no row move. The client repeats U1's guard question through public reads and leaves the decision to Rules.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. The screen origin, and so its browser key storage, now serves each later release of N that U1 admits in place. U1 keeps N's semantic identifier, definition and publisher, and `APPLICATION_TRUST` must list each release. Ruling d0a92549 moves the presentation review to that trust-list head, and `docs/operate-a-service.md` states the move where it describes the `SCREEN_HOSTS` rows. Every trust-list head now reviews a screen as well as a package, and checker reviews of those heads must read the release's presentation.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The install request and the upgrade share `installSelection`, `trustFor` and `submitRequest`, and the install's custody meaning does not change.\n\nFacts for the planner:\n- The sandbox and the room Workers change, so the landing needs a deployment with a rate read.\n- U4 must sign Counter 0.7.0 from a head that contains U3, as the note states. A screen built with an earlier client still compares the descriptor's presentation.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:be78eec47099c533feae69c08eb74807d9766187","binding":"assigned","head":"db5391979a051ba0443e54ba1dc15e8a715ee0dd","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8346e2a7770372f43b9f17a822b0eca96b99efb3\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4affdef0ba06564d1e33e54247e86f2a95fc2812\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8346e2a7770372f43b9f17a822b0eca96b99efb3","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}